From 9ef65839ebe2253d26b938c9491c49236a5d0eb6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slopdealer <326519127+slopdealer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:22:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/49] R8: restore builds the hard-link index in the first
 pass and looks every file up in it, as stock

The first pass kept a set without paths and the second pass rebuilt the
index while it ran, looking up only nodes that themselves report more than
one link. One inode recorded with one link on one path and with more on
another (a link added or removed during the backup) was restored as two
independent files; stock restores one hard-linked file. A path that records
one link can come before the path that records more, so the index has to be
complete before the second pass.

The first pass records the first path per inode again, and the second pass
uses stock's condition for every regular file, including the comparison
with the node's own path. With no indexed inode the lookup is skipped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
